/-!
# Alternating model restrictions for B.1.13

The pointwise Sylow-fixer bound is proved for every Aₘ with m ≥ 5, including
all A₆ automorphisms. It applies to perfect central covers and the actual
component containment argument. The subgroup-model conclusion is assembled
from the literal ambient intersection, conditional on the remaining intrinsic
classification of components in proper alternating Sylow overgroups.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), B.1.13,
printed p.74 (PDF p.85).
-/
